    --   OUT FishCast     (guid, {{ playerLocation, direction, strength }})
    --   IN  FishCast     (guid, { landed = b })     0.10-0.23s later; a Bobber appears
    --   IN  FishApproach ({ fish, to, time })       ~4.3s after the cast: a fish is
    --                                               swimming to the bobber and will
    --                                               reach it in `time` seconds
    --   IN  FishBite     ({ fisherData, fishEntry }) on arrival -- within 20ms of that
    --                                               prediction in three of the four,
    --                                               0.33s late in the fourth. 5.8-9.9s
    --                                               after the cast all told
    --   OUT FishCatch    ({ success = true })       4.58, 5.08, 5.53 and 5.65s after
    --                                               the bite: the minigame hold. The
    --                                               payload carries no proof of the
    --                                               minigame, only that it was won
    --   IN  ShowNotification ({ type = "ItemAdded", toolName = fishEntry.fishType })
    --                                               ~0.1s later; the fish is yours
    -- The engine never WAITS on FishApproach -- waiting for the bite itself beats
    -- waiting for a prediction of it -- but it listens, because it is the earliest
    -- sign a cast took at all: no bite with it seen is a fish that would not take,
    -- and no bite without it is a cast into empty water. That is the difference
